sentences.l:
“Arete, daughter of Rhexenor godlike,
both your husband and your knees I approach, having toiled much,
and these banqueters too;

to them may the gods grant blessed things
to live, and to his children may each one hand over
the possessions in his halls and the honour the people gave;

And late at last spoke among them the old hero Echeneus,
who indeed of the Phaeacian men was the elder
and in words excelled, knowing things old and many;

And hand-water a handmaid poured over them, bringing it in a pitcher,
a fine golden one, over a silver basin,
for washing;

for nothing else has ever been more dog-like than the hateful belly,
which by necessity bids one think of it,
even one greatly worn down and with grief in his heart,

And you, bestir yourselves at the appearing dawn,
so that you set me, the wretched one, on my fatherland,
even though having suffered much;

but he in the hall was left behind, heavenly Odysseus,
and beside him Arete and Alcinous godlike-in-form
sat;
